{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PUeQKyMTQGvaupNCBvcFmi","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"3c33f1642e679c593e4860e9e529e55c5b74645e","date":"2026-09-11T00:01:00+03:00","message":"(chore) O3-5964: Remove unreferenced SCSS files and dead AllergyFormTab component (#3638)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"solomonfortune","authorEmail":"solomonbuwule@gmail.com"},{"hash":"6de29927bd14a8cbe34db3aa522b14e2f4ef8df4","date":"2026-04-07T19:17:10+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-5540: Add quick-add allergy action to drug order basket (#3186)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Shravanthi","authorEmail":"147586547+Shravanthi20@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"72a1cd76ef5f2f4beb6351c9c21f8305b4e8c92b","date":"2026-03-19T15:14:40+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5512: Re-enable allergy delete button after failed deletion (#3132)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"omeri innocent","authorEmail":"innocentomeri08@gmail.com"},{"hash":"8ea84c53605bd7fcba910cbef4a9d187972d8816","date":"2026-02-26T20:14:13+03:00","message":"(fix) Remove redundant style overrides from allergy tags (#3063)","refs":"","body":"The .allergyLabel class was overriding several Carbon Tag defaults\nunnecessarily: display, border-radius, text-align, and padding. It also\nset margin on each tag while the parent container already used\ncolumn-gap, tripling the effective spacing between tags (~12px instead\nof 4px).\n\nRemove all redundant overrides so allergy tags use Carbon's native Tag\nlayout, keeping only the severity-based background colors. Switch the\nparent container from column-gap to gap so wrapped rows are also spaced\ncorrectly.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"6cd944f7d5c35862d6071c682ed3eb1223108801","date":"2026-02-13T02:14:09+03:00","message":"(feat) Add allergy pills display to drug search","refs":"","body":"- Add ExtensionSlot for allergy-list-pills-slot above search input\n- Add margin spacing to search input for better visual separation\n- Reorder Search component props alphabetically for consistency\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"54ddf9e5ecca4dc7e239e7362158ed58ee6fbc70","date":"2025-11-04T11:09:38+03:00","message":"(fix) Use correct translation namespace in allergies list extension","refs":"","body":"Fixes cross-app translation namespace for the allergies list extension\nby using the `translateFrom` function with the `moduleName` as the first\nargument instead of the `useTranslation` hook. This ensures that the translation\nstrings are loaded from the allergies app's namespace when the extension is\nrendered in other apps (e.g., medications app via the `allergy-list-pills-slot`\nextension slot).\n\nIt also removes unused `translateFrom` imports from conditions, lists, and\nprograms apps.\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f6f1914aac0316723c5f91c4a06b394c93aa01ca","date":"2025-09-22T12:06:21+01:00","message":"(feat) O3-5026: Allergy UI in Orders workflow (#2744)","refs":"","body":"* placeholder for allergy pills in drug order form\n\n* allergies-list component\n\n* use carbon tag component\n\n* O3-5026 Allergy UI in Orders workflow\n\n* 3/4 of changes suggested in review\n\n* 4/4 of changes suggested in review\n\n* Additional tweaks to allergy components\n\n- Rename allergy components to use .extension.tsx suffix following OpenMRS conventions\n- Update component names for consistency (allergiesTile, allergiesList)\n- Improve loading states with `TagSkeleton`\n- Add red tag styling for allergy visibility in medication workflow\n- Standardize \"Unknown\" fallback text across components\n- Adapt the delete allergy modal registration logic in the routes.json file","authorName":"Matt South","authorEmail":"matt@mattsouth.net"},{"hash":"b80ac03cf23adfab5e0e57a2f6bc5e3591e89352","date":"2025-06-17T19:56:27+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-3626: Allergen fields should be read-only when editing existing allergies  (#2462)","refs":"","body":"* feat: Add disabled state for allergens in allergy form and update styles\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* fixup\n\n* Make fields read-only on edit\n\n* Delete unused style\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"praneeth","authorEmail":"praneeth7077@gmail.com"},{"hash":"c038e67d4158fdf680ff1aadaad43a841a33f4c0","date":"2025-04-07T15:58:20+03:00","message":"(refactor) Improve allergy form initialization and loading states (#2347)","refs":"","body":"This commit addresses a critical issue where the allergy form would initialize with incorrect values when editing existing allergies. The problem occurred because:\n\n- Form initialization happened before allergic reactions were loaded from the server\n- Default values were only set once during form initialization\n- No loading state was shown while data was being fetched\n\nKey changes in this PR include:\n\n- Adding a loading state to the form that waits for allergic reactions to be loaded before initializing default values and rendering the form\n- Adding a ref to track initialization state to prevent the form from being rendered with incorrect values\n- Sorting the allergic reactions alphabetically by display name for improved readability and consistency\n- Adding a `CheckboxSkeleton` loading state to the form when allergic reactions are being loaded to prevent large layout shifts\n- Cleaning up the default value initialization logic for improved readability and maintainability\n","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"56861a24e4dcd9f52278e30cf7cd9293d78e4725","date":"2025-04-04T16:55:26+03:00","message":"(feat) Centralize allergy form validation logic (#2333)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) Centralize allergy form validation logic\n\nThis PR centralizes validation logic in the allergies form workspace so that the\nzod schema is the source of truth for validation rules. Presently, some validation logic exists in useEffect\nhooks that determines whether the submit button should be disabled. This logic isn't tied to any display logic, which means\nthat validation errors are not shown to the user when they are encountered.\n\nWith this PR, fields are validated when the user attempts to save or update an allergy. If validation fails, the user is presented with\nthe appropriate error message.\n\n* Update tests to account for new allergy form validation\n\nThis commit updates the AllergyForm test suite to account for the new allergy form validation logic. It also effects some useful refactoring to the allergy form workspace component. Notably, that includes inlining the AllergicReactionsForm component, annotating the zod schema with useful comments, and replacing enums with constants in line with best practices.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"548f8afcf734e0c7fbb87d6345e2490a528994cf","date":"2025-02-14T18:34:29+05:30","message":"(feat) O3-4342: Split allergy form fields (#2232)","refs":"","body":"* added openmrs datepicker\n\n* Improve error handling for comments in AllergyForm\n\n* replace openmrsDatePicker with cabon design datepicker\n\n* remove the onsetDate and kept only the comments\n\n* Correct label text casing for comments field in allergy form\n\n* updated en.json\n\n* updated en.json\n\n* fixup\n\n* removed onset date text in allergies.spec.ts\n\n* Rename 'comment' to 'comments' in allergy form schema and related logic\n\n* Refactor allergy form styling and improve form submission logic\n\n- Adds a loading state to the submit button when the form is being submitted\n- Fixes the form height to ensure the action buttons are pinned to the bottom of the form\n- Changes the `comments` form field name back to `comment` to match the backend data model\n- Fixes an issue where the allergic reactions from an existing allergy record were not correctly loaded into the form\nwhen editing.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>","authorName":"praneeth","authorEmail":"141117659+Muppasanipraneeth@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"5cab0737fca2e515f24eb53dbf1d2639519c0a26","date":"2025-01-28T18:47:28+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-4403: Unable to record allergy in non-English locale (#2215)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Unable to record allergy in non-English locale\r\n\r\n* Remove index","authorName":"Jayasanka Weerasinghe","authorEmail":"33048395+jayasanka-sack@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"f4566eef78a1864e280d9ca3f99b7505ae7d793c","date":"2024-07-09T14:33:59+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-3469: Fix allergy data tile display for severe allergies (#1897)","refs":"","body":"(fix) Fix allergy data tile display for severe allergies","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"d2a3c8afc7288a5d57a61ce2a469b7c16a2a8cfb","date":"2024-03-28T22:07:06+03:00","message":"(test) O3-3000: Add E2E tests for editing and deleting an allergy (#1761)","refs":"","body":"(test) O3-3OOO: Add E2E tests for editing and deleting an allergy","authorName":"Daud Kakumirizi","authorEmail":"dkakumirizii@gmail.com"},{"hash":"e438002a9b2012f6025a629c6b03a9ec1f65399f","date":"2024-03-07T22:31:31+03:00","message":"(feat) Add functionality to allow deleting and editing an allergy (#1703)","refs":"","body":"* Add functionality to allow deleting and editing an allergy\r\n\r\n(feat) O3-2760: Add a `closeWorkspaceWithSavedChanges` function to the workspace API (#1689)\r\n\r\n* Added new function 'closeWorkspaceWithSavedChanges' to close workspace after form is saved\r\n\r\n* Passing 'closeWorkspaceWithSavedChanges' as workspace props\r\n\r\n(docs) Amend steps for updating core libraries in README (#1690)\r\n\r\n(chore) Bump @openmrs/ngx-formentry (#1684)\r\n\r\n(fix) O3 2804: Reuse the ResponsiveWrapper component from esm-framework (#1673)\r\n\r\n* (feat) Reuse ResponsiveWrapper component from esm-framework\r\n\r\n* feat: Added Layer in visit-not