{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UynTtBxwNbw2CuA8fqdggk","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"f4b9490ba78fe5ee0be814d8b88c9cb67c183799","date":"2026-08-20T20:22:59+03:00","message":"(fix) Correct data handling defects in the generic obs widgets (#3587)","refs":"","body":"* (fix) Correct data handling defects in the generic obs widgets\n\nThe editable horizontal obs table discarded a typed value of 0 because\nthe save guard treated it as empty input. A numeric zero now saves;\nonly genuinely empty input bails.\n\nAn observation without an encounter crashed every widget built on\nuseObs, which dereferenced the FHIR encounter reference unguarded.\nObservation.encounter is optional in FHIR. Encounter-less obs now map\nwith no encounter and render as their own rows in the obs table. The\nmapping also no longer mutates the FHIR resources held in the SWR\ncache.\n\nA configured decimalPlaces of 0 was ignored because both tables tested\ndecimalPlaces > 0 and fell back to two decimal places. An explicit 0\nnow rounds to whole numbers.\n\nNumeric columns sorted incorrectly because integer values are stored as\nnumbers while fractional values are toFixed strings, and the comparator\ncompared them as strings. Numeric columns now compare numeric values.\n\n* (fix) Guard encounter type sorting against obs without an encounter\n\nEncounter-less obs now render as their own rows, so the encounter cell\ncan be undefined. Sorting the encounter type column called localeCompare\non it directly and crashed the widget. Coalesce to an empty string and\ncover it with a regression test that clicks the header.\n\n* (fix) Rename _validator to _validators in the obs widget config schemas\n\nThe config system only reads the plural key, so the inRange(0, 10)\nchecks on decimalPlaces never ran. With this rename, an out-of-range\ndecimalPlaces gets a validation error at startup instead of passing\nthrough silently.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"20cf33d04fe107ed4786f02904b7f64ec1c2b0ad","date":"2026-04-09T01:51:40+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-4648: Prevent crash when currentProvider is null (#2939)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Devarasetty Praneeth","authorEmail":"89689768+praneeth622@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"90dd0976ea0eed2f2aa4de749ba59cf16f02b097","date":"2026-04-02T00:43:58+03:00","message":"(fix) Handle missing encounters array in visit summary components","refs":"","body":"TestsSummary and VisitEncountersTable both call .map() on\nvisit.encounters without a fallback. If a visit has no encounters\narray, this throws at runtime. Default to an empty array in both\ncomponents to prevent the crash.\n","authorName":"denniskigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"8cfa2c6f1c106c7fac951b58ada21ad401e08b98","date":"2026-02-25T12:07:29+03:00","message":"(fix) Handle missing visit context in Angular form engine for visitless encounters (#3057)","refs":"","body":"The Angular form engine used `getPropOrThrow` for visit-related properties\n(`visitTypeUuid` and `visitUuid`) that are legitimately absent for\nvisitless encounters, causing it to crash with \"missing required Single\nSPA property\".\n\nThis was exposed by ebb3f1156 which correctly stopped falling back to\nthe active visit context when editing encounters, surfacing these latent\nbugs.\n\n- Pass visit context and patient from mapped encounter data to the form\n  widget slot in the encounters table\n- Change `getPropOrThrow` to `getProp` for `visitTypeUuid` in\n  `form-creation.service.ts` (wireDataSources)\n- Change `getPropOrThrow` to `getProp` for `visitUuid` in\n  `form-creation.service.ts` (setUpPayloadProcessingInformation),\n  `fe-wrapper.component.ts` (validateEncounterDatetimeWithVisit), and\n  `form-submission.service.ts` (submitEncounter)\n- Rename deprecated `browserTarget` to `buildTarget` in `angular.json`\n- Add tests for both visit-associated and visitless encounter scenarios","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5f21543d2885308d3f90a62a2aae0c82f4b2f5a8","date":"2025-10-10T19:49:16+03:00","message":"O3-5090 : Fix medication summary crash by removing external config dependency (#2775)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Donald Kibet","authorEmail":"chelashawdonald@yahoo.com"},{"hash":"7a49ac26795b571004a5c1a581dbe6358019f0d1","date":"2023-12-01T15:06:51-05:00","message":"(fix) Make it so visit diagnosis error doesn't crash the app (#1521)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Brandon Istenes","authorEmail":"bistenes@gmail.com"},{"hash":"98534acca5ed4f7e4c522725115391c726dc63fc","date":"2023-11-30T00:46:08-05:00","message":"(fix) O3-2612: Attachments App Crashes O3, then blocks adding attachments for any patient (#1515)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Brandon Istenes","authorEmail":"bistenes@gmail.com"},{"hash":"5529002efad11d760e678e14f1946e7a87c3a167","date":"2023-03-11T18:01:31+05:30","message":"(fix) Table styling fixes for data tables in patient chart (#1014)","refs":"","body":"* Table styling fixes (desktop and tablet) in past visits table\r\n\r\n* Table expansion padding fixed\r\n\r\n* Table styling improvements for Appointments\r\n\r\n* Table styling for biometrics table\r\n\r\n* Table styling for vitals table\r\n\r\n* Table styling for conditions table\r\n\r\n* Table styling for attachments table\r\n\r\n* Fine styling for attachments table header\r\n\r\n* Table styling for notes table\r\n\r\n* Conditioning fix in notes table\r\n\r\n* Table styling for forms table\r\n\r\n* Updated translations\r\n\r\n* Table styling for allergies table\r\n\r\n* Fixed failing test\r\n\r\n* Table styling for programs table\r\n\r\n* Fixed the stylings for icon based content switchers\r\n\r\n* Updated translations\r\n\r\n* Updated dependencies\r\n\r\n* Fixed crashing when editing an encounter","authorName":"Vineet Sharma","authorEmail":"sharmava05@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":8}"}]}]},